## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/null.html
- Summary (EN): Forwards each input to its matching output without altering the data. It works as a labelled collection point, so a named set of targets can be wired together.
- Résumé (FR) : Transmet chaque entrée numérotée vers la sortie correspondante sans la modifier, comme point de regroupement nommé pour un ensemble de cibles.

- Inputs meaning: ["input1, input2, and so on: numbered inputs, each passed to the output at the same position"]

- Key parameters: ["Set Fields from Inputs: fills the Output # parameters with the names of the connected inputs", "Output #: the name of each output; naming a wire changes the output name but not the internal input name"]

- Caveats: ["If an input is a cable, the first wire's name is used for the output name.", "A filled-in Output # name stays in place after its wires are removed, acting as a placeholder for future wiring.", "The page does not specify default output names or the maximum number of inputs."]

